ric, not willing to learn. For pilot, communication and learning are important. Might be concerning.\n\nCandidate B: very conscientious, handles stress well, good at assessing weather, excellent computer skills, regarded as pretentious, sometimes adopts wrong tone. Strengths: reliability, stress resilience, technical (weather, computer). Weaknesses: communication tone, pretentiousness (cooperation). Could be okay.\n\nCandidate C: anticipates dangerous situations, sees complex connections, excellent spatial vision, very good leadership, but unfriendly, eats unhealthily. Strengths: situational awareness, technical competence, leadership. Weaknesses: unfriendly (crew cooperation), health may affect reliability.\n\nCandidate D: responds to unexpected events adequately, concentrates well, solves problems extremely well, takes responsibility seriously, moody, loner. Strengths: problem solving, responsibility, concentration. Weaknesses: moodiness, loner (cooperation). Could be okay.\n\nWe need to start discussion, maybe propose Candidate B as leading due to reliability and stress handling, but note communication concerns. Or propose Candidate C for technical competence but note unfriendly. Choose one to start.\n\nLet's start with Candidate B as provisional recommendation, citing strengths and acknowledging concerns. Provide evidence. Also note that we still need to discuss others. Provide vote.\n\nProceed."}
